text:
Noah: quick design review note — the embedded help popover on the Integrations page keeps calling these objects 'handlers' but our docs and examples use 'endpoint'. watched a user click expecting 'endpoint' and get confused.
Yuki (Docs): thanks Noah. which popover? path please.
Noah: Console > Integrations > Webhook > Edit > Help (small inline popover). Title says 'Configure handler' and code examples show 'handler_id'. docs article is 'Create endpoint' and snippets use 'endpoint_id'.
Leo - Frontend: that'll break the in-app deep links because our popover link resolver looks up docs anchors by canonical slug. mismatch -> links jump to top of article or nowhere.
Yuki (Docs): suggestion: canonicalize on 'endpoint' in docs, and update popover copy to 'endpoint (aka handler)' for a short window. i'll add a one-line alias at top of the docs article and add anchor ids for the specific subheadings so popovers can target them precisely.
Ava (A11y): accessibility issue: the popover's doc links open the docs but we don't move focus or close the popover, so keyboard and screen-reader users lose context. need to close the popover, set aria-hidden=true on it, update hash, and programmatically focus the destination heading. also ensure the popover link has a meaningful aria-label.
Leo - Frontend: agreed. plan: on link click -> popover.hide(), popover.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true'), then after navigation focus target with tabindex='-1' + focus(). snippet we'll include in PR:
```
popover.hide();
popover.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
setTimeout(() => {
  const el = document.getElementById(targetId);
  if (el) {
    el.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
    el.focus();
    history.replaceState(null, '', `#${targetId}`);
  }
}, 100);
```
Yuki (Docs): i'll also add a small 'open full docs' icon in the popover that deep-links to the exact anchor. proposal: same-tab navigation so we maintain console context; if we go new-tab, aria-label must say '(opens in new tab)'.
Noah: can we also add a tiny transitional tooltip text inside the popover that reads 'handler is the same as endpoint' so users seeing 'handler' won't be thrown off until we complete the sweep?
Ava (A11y): if you add tooltip, make it accessible: either visible text or an aria-describedby pointing to a hidden live region. do not rely on hover-only hints.
Leo - Frontend: adding analytics event 'popover_doc_link' with {source:'popover', termShown:'handler', target_slug} so we can measure how often users hit mismatched terms.
Yuki (Docs): i'll run a doc search for 'handler' and produce a list of affected pages. plan: short-term alias + popover copies; medium-term full replacement to 'endpoint' across docs and UI.
Noah: can someone open a ticket with clear acceptance criteria: 1) popover copy updated to include 'endpoint' parenthetical; 2) add deep-link icon that targets section anchor; 3) focus management & aria-hidden behavior on navigation; 4) analytics event; 5) docs alias line and mapping spreadsheet.
linker-bot: created INFR-5122: "Popover lexicon clean-up: handler->endpoint + deep-link a11y" assigned to Leo - Frontend, due 6 days.
Yuki (Docs): thanks — i'll PR the alias text and share the list of 'handler' hits. will also add canonical meta for quicker slug detection.
Noah: awesome, thanks all :raised_hands:
